<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vlissingen</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Flushing</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vlissingen (Flushing in English) is a port city on the former island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/walcheren">Walcheren</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> province of Zeeland, at the mouth of the Western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scheldt">Scheldt</a>. Its capture by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sea-beggars">Sea Beggars</a> in April 1572 was one of the first successes of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-revolt">Dutch Revolt</a>. Later a base for privateers and the Dutch navy, it was the birthplace of Admiral <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michiel-de-ruyter">Michiel de Ruyter</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vlissingen.jpg" alt="Vlissingen" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vlissingen at Dutch Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Boulevard_Vlissingen.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
